#
# The REUSE tool the reuse job of .gitlab-ci.yml runs (build/ci/reuse-lint.sh: reuse
# lint, every file's copyright and licence known, REUSE Specification 3.3; CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Code style and licence headers"), by hand-chosen version. build/ci/reuse-requirements.txt is made from this file,
# with every package it pulls in pinned and every file's SHA-256, and that is the
# file the job installs from (pip --require-hashes).
#
# PyPI has no wheel of reuse for Python 3.14 (its 6.x wheels are tagged cp310
# alone), so pip builds it from its sdist, whose build backend is poetry-core: that
# comes from build/ci/reuse-build-requirements.txt, hashed the same way and
# installed first, and the job builds reuse with --no-build-isolation, so that the
# backend is not fetched by pip's isolation at whatever version PyPI serves that
# minute. python-magic needs libmagic, which the job installs from Debian
# (libmagic1t64), and the job names it as the encoding module
# (REUSE_ENCODING_MODULE=python-magic), so that a missing libmagic fails the job
# rather than leaving reuse on another module.
#
# To move to a newer reuse, change the version here and regenerate both locked
# files with uv, in the python:3.14-slim-trixie image the job runs in:
#
#   python3 -m venv /tmp/uv && /tmp/uv/bin/pip install uv
#   /tmp/uv/bin/uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.14 \
#       --output-file build/ci/reuse-requirements.txt build/ci/reuse-requirements.in
#   /tmp/uv/bin/uv pip compile --generate-hashes --python-version 3.14 \
#       --output-file build/ci/reuse-build-requirements.txt build/ci/reuse-build-requirements.in
#
# then put this file's three header lines back at the top of each output, keep
# poetry-core's pin within the range the new sdist's [build-system] requires, and
# run the job's script (.gitlab-ci.yml, reuse) on the tree.
reuse==6.2.0
